# The signed non-installing boot of the installer medium.
#
# Live is an AFFIRMATIVE mode, not "Install minus the autoinstall word": the UKI
# seals `neuralice.live=1` AND `systemd.unit=neural-ice-live.target`, and the
# early runtime generator accepts only that exact pair inside a closed sealed
# grammar. Before this target existed, MEDIA_MODE=live sealed no selector at all,
# so the medium fell through to the inherited installed-appliance default --
# which hard-requires the first-boot TPM ceremony (RequiredBy=multi-user.target)
# and drove a pristine Live boot into emergency.
#
# 🔴 THIS TARGET PULLS THE BASE SYSTEM AND ONE READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC SUMMARY.
# multi-user.target is exactly the edge that carries the installed ceremony, and
# neural-ice-installer.target is the destructive one. Requiring basic.target and
# nothing else is what keeps Live free of both.
#
# neural-ice-live-diagnostics.service is the mode's only product surface, and it
# is deliberately a Wants=, not a Requires=: a summary that fails must not take
# the boot with it, because on a medium with no login there is nothing to fall
# back to. That service takes no input, opens no listener, writes nothing and is
# forbidden IP traffic outright; see its unit file for why each bound is there.
#
# Any OTHER Requires=/Wants= added here -- an installed-appliance unit, a
# login/session surface, or the installer -- is a new access path on a medium
# whose whole safety argument is that it has none.
# image/test-installer-systemd-lifecycle.sh enumerates this dependency set
# exactly and refuses any addition to it.
[Unit]
Description=Neural ICE signed non-installing live boot (read-only diagnostics)
Documentation=https://github.com/Neural-ICE/ICE-CoreOS
Requires=basic.target
Wants=neural-ice-live-diagnostics.service
After=basic.target neural-ice-live-diagnostics.service
Conflicts=neural-ice-installer.target neural-ice-autoinstall.service
AllowIsolate=yes
